        },
        {
          "type": "page",
          "slug": "theorem-pythagorean_3_4_5",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "tag": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Straight-line distance is Pythagorean: the range over a 3-east, 4-north leg is 5 — 3² + 4² = 5². The oldest fix in navigation, exact."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "3^2 + 4^2 = 5^2"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "theorem pythagorean_3_4_5 : 3^2 + 4^2 = 5^2 := by decide"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page",
          "slug": "theorem-compass_rose_eight",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "tag": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "The compass rose is ℤ/8: eight principal headings, 45° apart — 8 · 45 = 360. The heading group is the same eight-fold ring the vortex turns on."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "8 * 45 = 360"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "theorem compass_rose_eight : 8 * 45 = 360 := by decide"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page",
          "slug": "theorem-reverse_bearing_involution",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "tag": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "The reciprocal (back) bearing is +4 on the ℤ/8 rose — 180° — and applying it twice returns the heading: (d + 4 + 4) mod 8 = d. Reverse of reverse is the original course; a reflection, like dz."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "(List.range 8).all (fun d => (d + 4 + 4) % 8 == d)"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "theorem reverse_bearing_involution : (List.range 8).all (fun d => (d + 4 + 4) % 8 == d) := by decide"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page",
          "slug": "theorem-quarter_turn_order_four",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "tag": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "A 90° turn is +2 on the ℤ/8 rose, and four of them box the compass back to the start: (d + 2·4) mod 8 = d — the quarter turn has order 4."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "(List.range 8).all (fun d => (d + 2*4) % 8 == d)"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "theorem quarter_turn_order_four : (List.range 8).all (fun d => (d + 2*4) % 8 == d) := by decide"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page",
          "slug": "theorem-dead_reckoning_adds",
          "children": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "tag": "h2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Dead reckoning is the vector sum of the legs: 4 east, 3 east, 2 west nets 4 + 3 − 2 = 5 east. Position is the running sum of displacements, exactly."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "([4, 3, -2] : List Int).sum = 5"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "language": "lean",
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "theorem dead_reckoning_adds : ([4, 3, -2] : List Int).sum = 5 := by decide"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  }
